      "topic": "Actual kernel symmetry",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The pinned kernel is invariant under simultaneous S1 rotation, not arbitrary radial transformations. Rotation averaging with the actual complex-disc submean inequality gives convolution domination. Its nonnegative normalized shrinking support gives the upper bound and pointwise convergence. Boundedness of the actual local potentials justifies Fubini directly."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Exact gluing sandwich",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "At a fixed point choose an inner chart, whose cutoff is zero. The source le_glue gives psi<=f_j,t<=psi_t. For every active chart, the overlap error contributes at most epsilon and its cutoff is nonpositive; glue_le contributes at most one more epsilon. Thus psi_t<=f_j,t+2epsilon. The chosen inner chart is independent of t."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Global boundedness and L1",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "Compactness of the finitely many closures of intermediate charts gives fixed compact convolution neighborhoods. The bounded potential and smooth reference potentials then give a common bound. No continuity of the original bounded cusp potential is assumed."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Near-semipositivity in the original class",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "The actual BRegWeightLevi theorem gives error 4 C_eta e1(t) in every intermediate chart. Finite compact chart comparisons give a global error against a fixed K\u00e4hler form. Every strictly positive correction is therefore eventually positive; the uncorrected reference need not be K\u00e4hler."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Energy convergence",
      "result": "PASS",
      "details": "For fixed positive correction choose one smooth positive representative from the sequence. The original approximants dominate the bounded limiting potential and converge in L1. Monotonicity and upper semicontinuity sandwich their unnormalized energies. Changing the fixed smooth reference adds a constant and does not change the convergence."
    },
    {
      "topic": "Actual source application",
      "result": "PASS",
